### Rotating Card (Hover Effect)

Below is a minimal example of an interactive “card” that flips/rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML** and **CSS** – no JavaScript.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
  /* Container that holds the card */
  .card-wrapper {
    perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
  }

  /* The card itself */
  .card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Allows children to be positioned in 3D space */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;/* Smooth animation */
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* Front side of the card */
  .card .front,
  .card .back {
    backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide backside while rotating */
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  }

  .card .front {
    background: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    color: #333;
  }

  .card .back {
    background: #3498db;
    color: #fff;
    transform: rotateY(180deg);     /* Place back side behind front */
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }

  /* Hover effect – rotate the whole card */
  .card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
  }
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front content -->
    <div class="front">
      <p>Front Side</p>
    </div>
    <!-- Back content -->
    <div class="back">
      <p>Back Side</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Sets the *perspective* so the rotation looks 3‑dimensional. |
| `.card` | Holds both sides; `transform-style: preserve-3d` allows its children to keep their 3D positions. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Each side of the card. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that’s turned away from the viewer. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on `.back` | Positions the back side behind the front. |
| `transition: transform 0.6s ease` | Animates the rotation smoothly. |
| `:hover` on `.card` | Triggers the rotation when the mouse hovers over the card. |

Feel free to replace the text with images or other content, adjust colors, size, or add more complex animations. Enjoy!
